/-!
# Two formulations of the acyclic models theorem

This file contains statements, rather than proofs, of:

1. the basis-and-models formulation used by the Lean 3 Brouwer fixed-point
   development;
2. a categorical comparison theorem relative to a class of model-projective
   objects.

The second statement uses augmented complexes.  When the augmentation object
is identified with zeroth homology, it says the same thing as lifting a map on
zeroth homology.
-/

noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Representable CategoryTheory.Functor

universe u w

namespace AcyclicModels

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{w} C]
variable {R : Type w} [CommRing R]


/--
The native representation of a naturally varying chain complex: a chain
complex in the functor category.  Its objectwise interpretation is
`K.asFunctor : C ⥤ ChainComplex (ModuleCat R) ℕ`.
-/

abbrev FunctorComplex :=
  ChainComplex (C ⥤ ModuleCat R) ℕ

